Core Difference between the ClusterIP and NodePort

ClusterIP : Only Inside the kubernetes cluster
NodePort  : Outside the cluster via node ip 


ClusterIP

Ex: 

type: ClusterIP

This creates : 
* internal virtual IP
* internal DNS
* internal load balancing 

But : "NOT REACHABLE FROM BROWSER / INTERNETE DIRECTLY"

example: backend-service

can be accessed by: 

>> http://backend-service:3000

only from: 
*Pods 
*Container inside cluster

NOT from your laptop browser


Why this is used: 
  Because pods like backend is a internal microservice and you  don't 
  * User directly calling backend pods
  * DB exposed publicly 
This is a secure architecture

___________________________________________________________________________
NodePort: 

Ex: 

type: NodePort

This exposes service externally 
kubernetes exposes a port on every node.
>> <NodeIP>:30691

Now browser/external users can access the pods by using the nodeip and the node port that is opened 

Browser
   ↓
NodeIP:30691
   ↓
frontend-service
   ↓
frontend pod





